<title>HONG KONG: King Fook interim profit rises 20.47 pct.</title>
<headline>King Fook interim profit rises 20.47 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   2.0    vs  1.7</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0    vs  1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    8.75   vs  7.26</p>
<p>    Turnover		     743.60 vs  813.15</p>
<p>    Company name		 King Fook Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 7-9, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 17, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - King Fook is a retailer of jewellery, watches and gold ornaments and engages in bullion trading and foreign exchange services.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
